# What `tauri dev` should NOT treat as a change to the app (gitignore syntax).
#
# Every change it sees kills the running app, rebuilds the crate and relaunches the window —
# 40 to 70 seconds with no window, or a boot splash, per event. Editors and coding agents save
# by writing a temporary file and renaming it over the real one, and each temporary file was an
# event of its own: the dev log showed a rebuild for `src/core/.!34894!api_server.rs`, a file
# that exists for a moment and holds nothing the build reads. The rename that follows is the
# real change, and it still triggers a rebuild.

# Atomic-write temporaries (`.!<pid>!name`), editor swap and backup files.
.!*!*
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.#*
*.tmp
.DS_Store
